{
  "_comment": [
    "Version numbers a schema writes into its own prose, pinned to the $id they were read under.",
    "An entry is a claim that a human read those sentences at that version -- not a claim that",
    "they are true. check:schema-self-reference recomputes the fingerprint and fails when the",
    "$id moves or a version-bearing sentence is edited, because a bump is the one event that can",
    "turn a correct sentence like 'Added in 1.2.0' into a wrong one like 'this schema is at 2.0.0'.",
    "Regenerate with `npm run ack:schema-self-reference` AFTER re-reading what it prints."
